.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga13_1985__ci09.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Voting rights of Elders and Deacons Emeriti after BCO 24-9 amendment","year":1985,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga13_1985__ci09.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga13_1985__ci09.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-9--inquiry:inquiries/ga13_1985__ci09.md:occ-04399dd10638","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga13_1985__ci09.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga13_1985__ci09.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/inquiries_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga13_1985__ci09.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"summary":"The CCB noted that the Twelfth GA amended BCO 24-9 to prohibit Emeriti from voting, while a grandfather clause preserved prior voting privileges for those already holding them."}},{"id":"bco:24-9--case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Bowen v. Eastern Carolina Presbytery","year":1991,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-9--case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.md:occ-41b7b823d0b7","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.html","repository_path":"cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["infant baptism","limited atonement","fundamentals of the system of doctrine","officer ordination","annulment of ordination","rescinding prior actions","subscription to confessional standards","ruling elder qualification","deacon qualification","covenant theology","TULIP","five points of Calvinism","original jurisdiction","suspension from office without due process","Robert's Rules rescind motion"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["1990-8"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Bowen challenged Presbytery’s attempt, two years after installation, to rescind its earlier ruling and annul local officers’ elections and ordinations without trial. The SJC sustained the complaint: ordination is perpetual, deposition requires judicial process, and rescission was out of order after implementation; Presbytery likewise could not suspend a local elder without due process. But it affirmed that infant baptism and limited atonement are fundamentals admitting no officer exception. The officers remained in office but doctrinally out of accord; voluntary demission or proper process was advised."}},{"id":"bco:24-9--overture:ga43_2015:8","record_id":"overture:ga43_2015:8","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 13-2, 34-10, 24-7 and 24-9 Regarding Ministers, Ruling Elders, and Deacons Without Call","year":2015,"disposition":"Answered in the negative","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga43_2015.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga43_2015.md","evidence_basis":"overture_action_target","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-9--overture:ga43_2015:8:occ-6a53cca44565","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga43_2015.html#ga43-p612","repository_path":"markdown/ga43_2015.md#ga43-p612